# Painterly Window-Lit Bakery Interior

Status: DONE
Milestone: M31 Warm hand-painted room and baked daylight
Dependencies: 29_GROUNDED_PAINTED_BAKERY_SCENE.todo

## Purpose

The owner supplied four bakery references and reiterated a hand-painted animated-film
art direction, especially beautiful sunlight coming from a window. The grounded
room is retained, but its material, composition and lighting need a stronger revision.

## Tasks

- [x] Record the latest reference direction without copying characters or artwork.
- [x] Assign an isolated candidate workspace so notebook builds remain safe.
- [x] Refine original wood, plaster, bakery objects and richly stocked shelves.
- [x] Add coherent fixed-window sunlight, cast shadows, contact shading and warm bounce.
- [x] Preserve strong camera look-around, floor support and readable display glass.
- [x] Render wide, portrait and short static posters from the same updated room.
- [x] Check geometry, real lighting, resources, viewport fitting and entry fallbacks.
- [x] Refresh the entrance campaign pair and publish only scoped reviewed output.

## Acceptance criteria

- Warm layered painted surfaces and bakery detail, not only a renamed shader.
- Window light stays fixed in world space and respects opaque occluders.
- Counter footing meets the floor, with visible contact shading and coherent perspective.
- No copied film characters, signs, wreath composition or reference pixels.
- Existing touch, skip, gesture-only bell, reduced-motion and resource fallbacks remain.
- Preserve all real product media, notebook work, header/roof and local cream experiment.
- No image-tool views or claims of aesthetic perfection or owner acceptance.

